---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Everyday command-line tools"
  description="A Rust command-line collection for downloads, reminders, file tasks, and time formatting."
  current="home"
>
  <section class="shell hero">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">A Rust command-line toolkit</p>
      <h1>Everyday tools for <span>your terminal.</span></h1>
      <p class="lead">Download files, set reminders, manage paths, and format time with one command.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button-primary" href="/install/">Install daily</a>
        <a class="button-link" href="/docs/">Read the docs →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="terminal" aria-label="daily command examples">
      <div class="terminal-head"><span class="dots">● ● ●</span> daily</div>
      <pre><span class="comment"># download a file</span>
<span class="prompt">$</span> daily download https://example.com/report.pdf report.pdf

<span class="comment"># set a reminder</span>
<span class="prompt">$</span> daily remind "Take a break" --at 2026-11-01T18:30:00+03:00

<span class="comment"># format a duration</span>
<span class="prompt">$</span> daily time duration 3665
1h 1m 5s</pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Commands</p><h2>Common everyday tasks.</h2></div>
        <p>One executable keeps everyday terminal jobs in a consistent command tree.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card"><span class="card-icon">01 / download</span><h3>Track a download</h3><p>See progress, transfer speed, and file size while an HTTP or HTTPS download runs.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><span class="card-icon">02 / remind</span><h3>Set a reminder</h3><p>Wait for a time and get a desktop notification from the running command.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><span class="card-icon">03 / file + time</span><h3>Manage common tasks</h3><p>Copy, move, rename, create directories, and format dates or durations.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell install-band">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Get started</p><h2 class="install-title">Install with Cargo.</h2><p>Rust toolchain required</p></div>
      <a class="button-primary" href="/install/">See installation steps</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
